CONCLUSIONS
  1. On the desk surface the suite gates, Account BREACHES Tier-1 for every query shape tested
     (A 3.340 ms, B 2.698 ms, C 3.284 ms vs 1.50 ms ceiling); the remaining 14 cutover doctypes are
     compliant at 0.65-1.10 ms on the identical harness.
  2. The breach is NOT cutover-induced: S3 measured 3.075 ms before the dry-run and 3.123 ms
     after it - identical within run-to-run noise, and no cutover step touches Account SQL.
  3. The ADR Section 4 pin (Account native 1.322 / governed 1.482 ms) was calibrated on the
     synthetic fixture prefix CT-T3- over a handful of fixture rows; at 2102 live Account rows
     the same methodology returns the values printed above, so the frozen pin does not transfer
     to production query text.
  4. For Arabic query text the ADR comparative ratio cannot be computed honestly (field-scope
     mismatch, section [3]); for ASCII query text both legs are reported above with their match-set
     sizes so the reader can judge comparability directly.
  5. Disposition: carried in latency-baseline.json as compliant:false and gated by baseline x 1.25;
     reported every run as S3-absolute ADVISORY. Owner decision required (runbook section 10, item 5).

This file contains no Arabic codepoints (verified by the repository-wide work-item scan in gates.log).

